      ],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "r34l1sm, SCENE 1 — QUESTION 1 (THE RED PLANET)\n\n\nAuthentic modern VLOG-style video featuring the male character from <Picture 1> as the trivia host. Use <Picture 1> as the exact visual reference for the host's face, hairstyle, clothing, body proportions, and overall identity throughout the video.\n\nNatural handheld smartphone-camera energy, realistic lighting, casual creator-style framing, expressive reactions, quick dynamic camera movements, and energetic social-media trivia pacing.\n\nIMPORTANT VIEWER INTERACTION RULE:\nThe male character from <Picture 1> speaks DIRECTLY TO THE VIEWER with a natural MALE FILIPINO-ACCENTED ENGLISH VOICE. The accent should sound authentic and conversational, not exaggerated or comedic. The camera represents the viewer. The host maintains direct eye contact with the camera whenever speaking.\n\n[Shot 1 — 0:00–0:05]\n\nStart outside at a scenic rocky lookout during golden hour.\n\nHandheld selfie-style medium shot.\n\nThe host walks slowly toward the camera while holding it at arm's length. Warm sunlight hits one side of his face. He suddenly stops, raises one eyebrow, and points directly toward the lens.\n\nThe camera makes a quick energetic digital punch-in as he asks the question.\n\nHOST:\n<d>[English, Male Filipino Accent] Okay, let's see how good your random trivia really is. Which planet is known as the Red Planet?</d>\n\nThe host immediately stops speaking and waits.\n\n[Shot 2 — 0:05–0:10]\n\nNo dialogue. Five-second viewer countdown.\n\nThe camera switches from selfie framing to a stable medium shot.\n\nPlace the host slightly LEFT-OF-CENTER.\n\nReserve completely clean negative space in the UPPER-RIGHT portion of the frame.\n\nMINIMAX H3 OPTIMIZED TIMER:\nDisplay exactly ONE enormous bold WHITE number in the upper-right negative space.\n\nNO timer box.\nNO circle.\nNO progress ring.\nNO progress bar.\nNO clock icon.\nNO extra text.\nNO duplicated numbers.\nNO decorative UI.\n\nOnly ONE bare number is visible at any moment.\n\nThe number must be pure bright white #FFFFFF.\n\nUse a very thick, heavy, geometric sans-serif font with clean straight edges.\n\nThe number occupies approximately 20% of the total frame height.\n\nThe number is perfectly centered within the upper-right empty area.\n\nThe number changes instantly with a HARD VISUAL CUT every exactly one second:\n\n5\nthen 4\nthen 3\nthen 2\nthen 1\n\nNever display two numbers simultaneously.\n\nAUDIO SYNCHRONIZATION RULE:\nExactly ONE short, dry mechanical \"CLICK\" sound occurs at the exact instant each new number appears.\n\nNo echo.\nNo reverb.\nNo spoken countdown.\nNo background music during the countdown.\n\nTIMELINE:\n\nAt 5:\n[AUDIO: One sharp CLICK]\nA giant WHITE \"5\" appears.\nHost crosses his arms and confidently stares into the camera.\n\nAt 4:\n[AUDIO: One sharp CLICK]\nThe \"5\" disappears completely and is instantly replaced by a giant WHITE \"4\".\nHost tilts his head and raises one eyebrow.\n\nAt 3:\n[AUDIO: One sharp CLICK]\nThe \"4\" disappears completely and is instantly replaced by a giant WHITE \"3\".\nHost taps his temple twice with his index finger.\n\nAt 2:\n[AUDIO: One sharp CLICK]\nThe \"3\" disappears completely and is instantly replaced by a giant WHITE \"2\".\nHost leans toward the camera with an exaggerated suspicious expression.\n\nAt 1:\n[AUDIO: One sharp CLICK]\nThe \"2\" disappears completely and is instantly replaced by a giant WHITE \"1\".\nHost suddenly grins as if he knows the viewer has locked in an answer.\n\nNO SPOKEN COUNTDOWN.\n\n[Shot 3 — 0:10–0:13]\n\nThe number \"1\" disappears completely.\n\nSMASH CUT.\n\nThe host is now standing in a dramatic red rocky desert environment resembling the surface of Mars.\n\nStrong wind lightly blows his shirt and hair.\n\nA huge dark charcoal rectangular answer card snaps into the empty space beside him.\n\nThe card contains exactly ONE line of enormous bold WHITE uppercase text:\n\nMARS!\n\nNo other text appears.\n\nThe camera rapidly pushes toward the host.\n\nHOST:\n<d>[English, Male Filipino Accent] Mars! Iron minerals in the soil are what give it that famous rusty red color!</d>\n\n[Shot 4 — 0:13–0:15]\n\nThe host smiles confidently and gives the camera a thumbs-up.\n\nSuddenly, an enormous dusty wind gust blasts across the frame from right to left.\n\nThe host's eyes widen.\n\nThe wind violently blows him sideways out of frame.\n\n[AUDIO: Powerful WHOOSH]\n\nThe camera shakes briefly from the impact.\n\nHard cut."
      ],
